  "body": "Found in the reads of PR #2515 (the Mach3 Mill post). These items are owed polish. They are not defects of the posted program.\n\n1. `assets/posts/mach3.cps` does not declare `explains = \"paren\"`. Explain G-code is refused by name for a Mach3 program. grblHAL, Mach4 and LinuxCNC declare it.\n2. `G86` with a dwell of zero writes no `P` word. Mach3 is, on purpose, not in the table `ZERO_DWELL_P0`. No public Mach3 source in the script's provenance pins that choice. Check \"Using Mach3Mill\" (10.7.24.7) and record the fact in the script comment and in a test.\n3. The option `dwellInMilliseconds = true` has no golden and no test. Add a test that pins `P500` for a dwell of 0.5 s on `G82`.\n\nWork this issue after PR #2515 merges.\n",
